b. In requested order y=1,3,6,7.1,0.5:
   exact x=0,1,ln(6)/ln(3),ln(7.1)/ln(3),ln(0.5)/ln(3);
   decimals 0,1,1.6309298...,1.7841552...,-0.6309298...;
   graph readings about 0,1,1.6,1.8,-0.6.
c. Because 3^x increases:
   3^x>5 has exact solution x>ln(5)/ln(3)=1.4649735...;
   graph boundary about 1.5, with open endpoint.
   3^x<1 has exact solution x<0, open endpoint.
   A rounded graph boundary is not the exact threshold.
   Do not mark a scan-read decimal or rounded inequality as an exact
   string answer merely because algebra can supply an exact benchmark.

630 / binding fig-74 / SOLVED
For x>0: 1.3^x < 3^x < 4.5^x.
For x<0: 4.5^x < 3^x < 1.3^x.
At x=0 all equal 1. General rule: a larger base gives a higher graph
to the right of the y-axis and a lower graph to its left.
This is a comparative/explanatory graph response; retain ungraded
unless a separately authored reliably judgeable interaction exists.

